  "review": {
    "templates": "Every evaluation, hit or miss, runs runCached -> createScriptRecord(realm, inherited, literals): a fresh Script record and therefore fresh template sites per evaluation (the native compiler resolves sites through the per-parse carrier; managedTemplateSites runs on every compile). Native case 'template-identity' checks a !== b across evaluations, loop and function evaluations distinct, and sharing within one evaluation (r[0] === r[1]); corpus program 'templateSites' checks the same against Node. Hosts whose entries instantiate template recipes per compile are not marked reusable (lowered Node host), so they never retain such entries.",
    "functions": "Functions are created by running the entry, so each evaluation creates fresh function objects; [[SourceText]] comes from the same source text. Corpus 'functionIdentity' (lowered host compiles once; native case) checks made[0] !== made[1], equal toString, toString text and behaviour against Node; 'freshFunctions' and 'closures' cover captured environments.",
    "hiddenInputs": "parseEvalScript and lowerDirectEvalScript read only the source text and the flags integer; the shape string is 'direct-eval:' + flags + ':' + privateEnvironment + ':' + fieldInitializer with the full flags integer. Flags: directEvalStrict (1, caller strictness), directEvalInFunction (2, new.target availability; arrows inherit their enclosing function's bit statically), directEvalInMethod (4, super property), directEvalInDerivedConstructor (8, super call), directEvalUnsupportedCapability (16, rejected before the cache), directEvalInClassFieldInitializer (32, arguments early error), directEvalInPrivateEnvironment (64, private-name resolution). Private names in scope are not lowering inputs: lowering threads the caller's private environment at run time and unresolved names raise SyntaxError when the entry runs (corpus 'privateNames': the same text in two classes with different private names compiles once; the second class still gets SyntaxError). Indirect eval and ShadowRealm have no caller inputs; their shapes are 'indirect-eval' and 'shadow-realm'.",
    "failures": "Only results of host.compile with ok and reusable are retained; parse errors, lowering early errors, compile failures (sticky unsupported) and empty bodies return before retention. Each failing evaluation re-parses and throws a fresh error object (corpus 'freshSyntaxErrors' for direct and indirect eval, 'syntaxErrorsRepeat'; compile counts 0).",
    "realms": "The cache lives in createEntryRunner's closure, one per evaluator; evaluators are created per realm and per ShadowRealm, and the runner's code domain is fixed and re-checked before every hit. Unit test 'eval source caches are per realm and per evaluator': two realms' direct evaluators and a ShadowRealm evaluator sharing one host compile three entries; records belong to the evaluating realm.",
    "memory": "Per entry: key string (shape about 25-30 units + separator + source <= 2048 units) as flat UTF-16 = 24-byte header + 2 bytes/unit, about 4.2 KB at the limit; literal table <= 64 strings whose values are slices of the source (<= 2048 units total, about 5.6 KB with headers) plus list storage (Test262 images use sparse-list nodes, about 48 B per element, about 3 KB); the CachedEvalSource record and LinkedMap entry/index about 0.2 KB. Worst case about 13 KB per entry and about 3.3 MB per evaluator at 256 entries; typical short eval sources are under 1 KB."
  },
